  "cross_tradition_view": "Most of these traditions would likely support avoiding damage to the tree and acting with consideration toward both neighbors; many would praise notice and an offer to remove the branches. They may split on whether cutting to the boundary without asking is itself wrong, with justice and respect for boundaries supporting the act and politeness, care, and compassion emphasizing consultation.",
